/* ============================================================================
   MODULE 01 — CORE CONCEPTS & ARCHITECTURE
   ============================================================================
   • A partitioned table is split into multiple physical units (partitions) based on values in one PARTITION COLUMN.
   • Partitioning is transparent to queries; SQL Server routes rows automatically.
   • Key Objects:
       PARTITION FUNCTION  → defines the boundary values & direction (LEFT/RIGHT)
       PARTITION SCHEME    → maps each partition to a filegroup
       TABLE / INDEX       → created ON the partition scheme
   • Max partitions per table: 15,000 (SQL Server 2012+)
   • Partition column must be NOT NULL (or NULLs go to partition 1).
   ============================================================================ */

